.TH CANDOR-GUI 1 "2026-11-15" "candor 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
candor-gui \- desktop client for the Candor process monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B candor-gui
[\fB\-\-replay\fR \fIFILE.frames.jsonl\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Candor desktop app. Three pages:
.TP
.B Processes
CPU, memory and events per second (with the number of events not
recorded), and every process with its CPU, memory, connections and score.
Click a process for its detail: an overview (charts, what it did, its
findings), an access map of everything it and its children touched, and
the raw events, files, connections, syscalls, children and memory maps.
.TP
.B Findings
Every finding, newest first, each with what happened, why it is flagged and
a harmless explanation.
.TP
.B Glasshouse
Run a program among decoy files and read a report of what it read,
changed, deleted and tried to reach. \fBTry an example\fR runs a three-line
demonstration script.
.PP
It talks to
.BR candord (8)
over its socket and needs membership in the \fBcandor\fR group. It refuses
to run as root. The fonts Inter and JetBrains Mono are compiled in (SIL Open
Font License; see /usr/share/doc/candor/fonts).
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B /
Search processes.
.TP
.B Esc
Back one level.
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down ", " Enter
Move in the process table and open the selected process.
.TP
.B f
Follow the selected process.
.TP
.BR Tab ", " Enter ", " + ", " \-
In the access map: focus the next node, select it, zoom.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-replay " FILE"
Show a saved recording (made with \fBcandor replay \-\-frames\fR) instead of
the live daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR candor (1),
.BR candord (8)
